{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "unitId": "chapter-when-moral-seriousness-scales-parts-part-3-the-pressure-point-chapter-7-the-acceleration-threshold",
  "generationHash": "sha256:001ee9f5eb2cb2e04543cd819262da1961da8750cfc8e77ec773b5a60de8d863",
  "granularity": "segment-only",
  "segments": [
    {
      "id": "s0001",
      "text": "Chapter 7: The Acceleration Threshold",
      "startMs": 0.0,
      "endMs": 2705.0,
      "charStart": 0,
      "charEnd": 37
    },
    {
      "id": "s0002",
      "text": "The Acceleration Threshold",
      "startMs": 3309.0,
      "endMs": 4934.0,
      "charStart": 38,
      "charEnd": 64
    },
    {
      "id": "s0003",
      "text": "As systems thin, restraint does not vanish immediately.",
      "startMs": 5538.0,
      "endMs": 9311.0,
      "charStart": 66,
      "charEnd": 121
    },
    {
      "id": "s0004",
      "text": "It becomes uneven.",
      "startMs": 9311.0,
      "endMs": 10600.0,
      "charStart": 121,
      "charEnd": 139
    },
    {
      "id": "s0005",
      "text": "For a time, actors continue to absorb cost, maintain contestability, and deliberate carefully.",
      "startMs": 10600.0,
      "endMs": 17183.0,
      "charStart": 139,
      "charEnd": 233
    },
    {
      "id": "s0006",
      "text": "The difference is not moral collapse but perceived disadvantage.",
      "startMs": 17183.0,
      "endMs": 21583.0,
      "charStart": 233,
      "charEnd": 297
    },
    {
      "id": "s0007",
      "text": "The acceleration threshold emerges when restraint begins to feel",
      "startMs": 22036.0,
      "endMs": 25948.0,
      "charStart": 302,
      "charEnd": 366
    },
    {
      "id": "s0008",
      "text": "selectively costly.",
      "startMs": 26065.0,
      "endMs": 27829.0,
      "charStart": 367,
      "charEnd": 386
    },
    {
      "id": "s0009",
      "text": "At this point, one actor absorbs friction while another moves quickly.",
      "startMs": 28212.0,
      "endMs": 33181.0,
      "charStart": 388,
      "charEnd": 458
    },
    {
      "id": "s0010",
      "text": "One side preserves contestability while another narrows it.",
      "startMs": 33507.0,
      "endMs": 37524.0,
      "charStart": 459,
      "charEnd": 518
    },
    {
      "id": "s0011",
      "text": "The asymmetry may be modest, but it is visible.",
      "startMs": 37524.0,
      "endMs": 40914.0,
      "charStart": 518,
      "charEnd": 565
    },
    {
      "id": "s0012",
      "text": "The experience is not outrage.",
      "startMs": 40914.0,
      "endMs": 43642.0,
      "charStart": 565,
      "charEnd": 595
    },
    {
      "id": "s0013",
      "text": "It is exposure.",
      "startMs": 44141.0,
      "endMs": 45430.0,
      "charStart": 598,
      "charEnd": 613
    },
    {
      "id": "s0014",
      "text": "Under these conditions, the temptation is rarely domination.",
      "startMs": 45755.0,
      "endMs": 49586.0,
      "charStart": 615,
      "charEnd": 675
    },
    {
      "id": "s0015",
      "text": "It is defense.",
      "startMs": 49586.0,
      "endMs": 51119.0,
      "charStart": 675,
      "charEnd": 689
    },
    {
      "id": "s0016",
      "text": "Research on competitive escalation shows that actors frequently mirror hardening behaviors not out of aggression but out of fear of unilateral vulnerability.",
      "startMs": 51491.0,
      "endMs": 61777.0,
      "charStart": 692,
      "charEnd": 849
    },
    {
      "id": "s0017",
      "text": "When reciprocity weakens, defensive imitation becomes rational.",
      "startMs": 61777.0,
      "endMs": 66456.0,
      "charStart": 849,
      "charEnd": 912
    },
    {
      "id": "s0018",
      "text": "What begins as self-protection can gradually resemble the very acceleration it sought to guard against.",
      "startMs": 66456.0,
      "endMs": 73991.0,
      "charStart": 912,
      "charEnd": 1015
    },
    {
      "id": "s0019",
      "text": "Hardening follows predictable patterns.",
      "startMs": 74606.0,
      "endMs": 77126.0,
      "charStart": 1019,
      "charEnd": 1058
    },
    {
      "id": "s0020",
      "text": "Discretion narrows.",
      "startMs": 77451.0,
      "endMs": 78902.0,
      "charStart": 1059,
      "charEnd": 1078
    },
    {
      "id": "s0021",
      "text": "Flexibility declines.",
      "startMs": 78902.0,
      "endMs": 80852.0,
      "charStart": 1078,
      "charEnd": 1099
    },
    {
      "id": "s0022",
      "text": "Trust is replaced by verification.",
      "startMs": 81235.0,
      "endMs": 83952.0,
      "charStart": 1101,
      "charEnd": 1135
    },
    {
      "id": "s0023",
      "text": "Processes become less forgiving.",
      "startMs": 83952.0,
      "endMs": 86506.0,
      "charStart": 1135,
      "charEnd": 1167
    },
    {
      "id": "s0024",
      "text": "These shifts are often justified as prudence.",
      "startMs": 87122.0,
      "endMs": 90605.0,
      "charStart": 1169,
      "charEnd": 1214
    },
    {
      "id": "s0025",
      "text": "Each decision appears reasonable in isolation.",
      "startMs": 90605.0,
      "endMs": 94100.0,
      "charStart": 1214,
      "charEnd": 1260
    },
    {
      "id": "s0026",
      "text": "Escalation rarely announces itself as a moral turn.",
      "startMs": 94100.0,
      "endMs": 97919.0,
      "charStart": 1260,
      "charEnd": 1311
    },
    {
      "id": "s0027",
      "text": "It presents as necessary adaptation.",
      "startMs": 98361.0,
      "endMs": 101193.0,
      "charStart": 1314,
      "charEnd": 1350
    },
    {
      "id": "s0028",
      "text": "Importantly, structural pressure increases the cost of restraint; it does not eliminate agency.",
      "startMs": 101704.0,
      "endMs": 108565.0,
      "charStart": 1352,
      "charEnd": 1447
    },
    {
      "id": "s0029",
      "text": "Actors still choose whether to imitate acceleration or absorb its disadvantage.",
      "startMs": 108565.0,
      "endMs": 114556.0,
      "charStart": 1447,
      "charEnd": 1526
    },
    {
      "id": "s0030",
      "text": "The threshold marks a change in incentives, not a removal of judgment.",
      "startMs": 114556.0,
      "endMs": 119734.0,
      "charStart": 1526,
      "charEnd": 1596
    },
    {
      "id": "s0031",
      "text": "The danger lies in normalization.",
      "startMs": 120315.0,
      "endMs": 122834.0,
      "charStart": 1600,
      "charEnd": 1633
    },
    {
      "id": "s0032",
      "text": "When defensive acceleration becomes habitual, it ceases to feel defensive at all.",
      "startMs": 122834.0,
      "endMs": 128662.0,
      "charStart": 1633,
      "charEnd": 1714
    },
    {
      "id": "s0033",
      "text": "It becomes baseline.",
      "startMs": 129115.0,
      "endMs": 130485.0,
      "charStart": 1716,
      "charEnd": 1736
    },
    {
      "id": "s0034",
      "text": "What was once an exception hardens into expectation.",
      "startMs": 130485.0,
      "endMs": 134966.0,
      "charStart": 1736,
      "charEnd": 1788
    },
    {
      "id": "s0035",
      "text": "At that point, escalation proceeds automatically.",
      "startMs": 134966.0,
      "endMs": 138682.0,
      "charStart": 1788,
      "charEnd": 1837
    },
    {
      "id": "s0036",
      "text": "The acceleration threshold is therefore the last clearly visible moment",
      "startMs": 139332.0,
      "endMs": 143523.0,
      "charStart": 1841,
      "charEnd": 1912
    },
    {
      "id": "s0037",
      "text": "of choice.",
      "startMs": 143581.0,
      "endMs": 144313.0,
      "charStart": 1913,
      "charEnd": 1923
    },
    {
      "id": "s0038",
      "text": "Before reflex sets in, actors can still recognize what is happening.",
      "startMs": 144823.0,
      "endMs": 149386.0,
      "charStart": 1925,
      "charEnd": 1993
    },
    {
      "id": "s0039",
      "text": "They can ask whether matching speed preserves stability or erodes it further.",
      "startMs": 149386.0,
      "endMs": 154425.0,
      "charStart": 1993,
      "charEnd": 2070
    },
    {
      "id": "s0040",
      "text": "They can decide whether disadvantage is intolerable—or whether preserving restraint has value beyond immediate symmetry.",
      "startMs": 154425.0,
      "endMs": 162413.0,
      "charStart": 2070,
      "charEnd": 2190
    },
    {
      "id": "s0041",
      "text": "Escalation is not inevitable.",
      "startMs": 162982.0,
      "endMs": 165025.0,
      "charStart": 2194,
      "charEnd": 2223
    },
    {
      "id": "s0042",
      "text": "It is incremental.",
      "startMs": 165199.0,
      "endMs": 166534.0,
      "charStart": 2224,
      "charEnd": 2242
    },
    {
      "id": "s0043",
      "text": "“There is a point where restraint feels selectively costly.",
      "startMs": 167231.0,
      "endMs": 170679.0,
      "charStart": 2244,
      "charEnd": 2303
    },
    {
      "id": "s0044",
      "text": "That point is dangerous—not because escalation is forced, but because it begins to feel rational.”",
      "startMs": 170679.0,
      "endMs": 176937.0,
      "charStart": 2303,
      "charEnd": 2401
    }
  ]
}
